cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use cTSEMO, cite this software release and the Bradford et al.
  TSEMO article identified in the preferred citation.
title: cTSEMO
abstract: >-
  A minimal sequential two-objective MATLAB extension of TSEMO for expensive
  problems observed through two objectives and one aggregate binary
  feasibility label.
type: software
authors:
  - name: cTSEMO contributors
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-08-09
license: BSD-2-Clause
keywords:
  - Bayesian optimization
  - constrained optimization
  - multiobjective optimization
  - Thompson sampling
  - binary feasibility
  - MATLAB
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  authors:
    - family-names: Bradford
      given-names: Eric
    - family-names: Schweidtmann
      given-names: Artur M.
    - family-names: Lapkin
      given-names: Alexei A.
  title: >-
    Efficient multiobjective optimization employing Gaussian processes,
    spectral sampling and a genetic algorithm
  journal: Journal of Global Optimization
  year: 2018
  volume: 71
  issue: 2
  start: 407
  end: 438
  doi: 10.1007/s10898-018-0609-2
